1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Linn Ullmann, originally Karin Beate Ullmann, (born 9 August 1966 in Oslo, Norway) is a Norwegian author and journalist.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Ullmann
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linn_Ullmann
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.snl.no/Linn_Ullmann
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.oktober.no/nor/forfattere/norske/ullmann_linn
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nytimes.com/2005/01/30/books/chapters/0130-1st-ullmann.html?_r=1
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nytimes.com/2008/08/17/books/review/DErasmo-t.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT Ullmann is the daughter of actress, author and director Liv Ullmann and director and screenwriter Ingmar Bergman. She is Liv Ullmann's only child and Bergman's youngest daughter, one of nine children Bergman fathered with five dif
2 CONC ferent women.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She studied literature for six years in New York, graduating from New York University in 1988.
2 CONT
2 CONT Work
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1992 she permanently moved back to her native Norway and began to work for the tabloid newspaper Dagbladet, one of Norway's leading newspapers. Eventually she became a newspaper journalist in Norway, and subsequently a successf
2 CONC ul author. She also is a well-known commentator in Norway's leading Conservative newspaper, Aftenposten, where she writes on political and cultural issues.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT As of 2005, she has written four novels, some of them translated into more than 30 languages, which have received critical acclaim also far outside Norway. Her debut novel, Before You Sleep was sold to 14 countries (including the 
2 CONC United States, Britain, France and Germany) before it was even published in Norway, a flying start rarely bestowed upon Norwegian authors.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2009, her novel A Blessed Child was nominated to the Independent Foreign Fiction Prize.[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal life
2 CONT
2 CONT Ullmann is married to Niels Fredrik Dahl, an award-winning Norwegian poet, novelist and playwright. They have one child. Ullmann also has a son from a previous marriage to a Norwegian lawyer, as well as two stepchildren. She lives
2 CONC  in a big flat on the West side of Oslo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Works
2 CONT
2 CONT Før du sovner (Before You Sleep, translated by Tiina Nunnally) (1998)
2 CONT
2 CONT Når jeg er hos deg (Stella Descending) (2001)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nåde (Grace) (2002)
2 CONT
2 CONT Et Velsignet Barn (A Blessed Child) (2005)
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT (snl.no) Linn Ullmann, født 9. august 1966, norsk forfatter og spaltist, datter av Liv Ullmann og Ingmar Bergman; gift med Niels Fredrik Dahl. Hun debuterte med romanen Før du sovner (1998) – en burlesk og fantasifull familieroman
2 CONC  med historien om en ung kvinnes forsøk på å vinne fotfeste i livet som hovedtråd. Romanen ble solgt til over tjue land allerede før den forelå. I hennes andre roman, Når jeg er hos deg (2001) står en ung kvinnes oppsiktsvekkende 
2 CONC og mystiske dødsfall i sentrum. Med romanen Nåde (2002) tar hun opp det vanskelige spørsmålet om selv å velge døden når sykdom gjør livet meningsløst. I Et velsignet barn (2005) handler det om tre unge kvinners forhold til en vans
2 CONC kelig far som bor langt borte på en øy, selv om barndomsopplevelser og -minner utgjør hovedsaken. Her berøres temaer som har vært sentrale i forfatterskapet – fortielse, lengsel, svik.
