1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''AGN1766, 15/12, §11:'''
2 CONT S:D: Afwa Byemän The innkeeper Olof Söderström, Mats Matsson, Jan Jansson, Erik Jonsson, Olof Nilsson, Erik Swensson, the widowed wife Margeta Andersdotter, were sued by Krono Länsmann Välaktad Anders Nygren not only because they 
2 CONC accused during what was then a severe drought, a fire was lit on Grannä--, whereby a forest fire started and spread 500 cubits in length and 210 cubits in width, as well as damaged forest to the value of 25 dalers, without also be
2 CONC ing responsible for a wild forest fire at Galtön, belonging to Afwa Village, where within a tract of 1950 alnars length and 900 alnars width to 100 pine trees and 100 spruce timbers was found after inspection burned up and lost to
2 CONC  the value of 80 dalers 8 öre kmt. In response to this, Afwa Byemän, excluding Söderström and the widow Margeta Andersdotter, explained that the cause of this later forest fire was completely unknown to them, but believed that fis
2 CONC hermen who had their feats at Galtön must have caused this fire, but to light the fire on Gräs --n, when the Afwa Boerne had their sheep, they confessed themselves guilty, and will unanimously agree to clear the mulbet in this way
2 CONC , considering that the fire would do no greater harm, than only overrun the land, which they most often added will try, but now of the slow and strong drought no better succeeded. Request for his release, to be able to confirm his
2 CONC  innocence to the forest fire that started on Galtön with Ed. It was certified that the innkeeper Söderström and the widowed wife Margeta Andersdotter no less than the other Afwa Byemäns in this and the previous case, concerning G
2 CONC räsön, had been agreed, but they had no reason to fail to report or show.
2 CONT Rash
2 CONT Because the innkeeper Söderström and his wife Margeta Andersdotter are also listed along with the other Afwa Boers for complicity in the forest fire that broke out on their property last summer and caused damage, because of all th
2 CONC ose present and heard the defendants on the same case, the Härads Court cannot finally express itself , future Söderström and Margeta Andersdotter now for non-appearance to 2 dalers Smt each case case, and should with the other ne
2 CONC ighbors next Ting at 5 dalers Smts fine stop and in the case explain
2 CONT
2 CONT '''AGN1766,15/12,§20:'''
2 CONT S:D: The innkeeper Välaktad Olof Söderström had agreed to his neighbors Mats Matsson, Jan Jansson, Erik Jonsson, Olof Nilsson, Nils Hansson and widowed wife Margeta Andersdotter for the next. verstid had taken 300 pieces of constr
2 CONC uction timber from the village's undisturbed forest for sale, which the defendants admitted. However, the same timber is still lying unsold in the forest, unless the Innkeeper has forbidden them to remove it. Regretfully, the defe
2 CONC ndant complained about the innkeeper as if he was trying to persuade them to use the forest, the last means they have of any support for themselves and their people, and the burden of their scapegoats, preferably their weak home a
2 CONC ffairs do not suggest anything, but the forest is abundant and sufficient, which and the board knew the certificate. They will also if the clearing took place duly announced Söderström, to deserve in the same way, even though cons
2 CONC iderable timber from the forest has been used for the rebuilding of his recently burned farm. Now, because of the demand, the innkeeper Söderström was not present, nor authorized by himself for the execution of his above-mentioned
2 CONC  lawsuit, nor did he notify the due date. Because the Court of Härads, in the capacity of 12 Cap: Rbl, that Söderström, for his non-appearance, made himself 2 Daler Smts fine due, and that his counterparties pay their travel expen
2 CONC ses. But as they have not made any such claim against him either, the Court of Appeals therefore lets it depend that Söderström must show his disrepair next time, and that he has not been able to announce it to the Court. Meanwhil
2 CONC e, Afwa Villagers have not taken their cut timber to lift and use.
