1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allvar_Gullstrand '''Allvar Gullstrand'''] (5 June 1862 – 28 July 1930) was a Swedish ophthalmologist and optician.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Landskrona, Sweden, Gullstrand was professor (1894–1927) successively of eye therapy and of optics at the University of Uppsala. He applied the methods of physical mathematics to the study of optical images and of the refr
2 CONC action of light in the eye. For this work, he received the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine in 1911.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gullstrand is noted also for his research on astigmatism and for improving the ophthalmoscope and corrective lenses for use after removal of a cataract from the eye.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was elected a member of the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences in 1905, and served on the Academy's Prize Committee for Physics. While serving on the committee, he used his position to block Einstein from receiving a Nobel Prize
2 CONC  in Physics for his theory of relativity, which Allvar believed to be wrong.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gullstrand married Signe Breitholtz (1862-1946) in 1885 and died in Stockholm where he was interred at Norra begravningsplatsen.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://et.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allvar_Gullstrand
2 CONT
