1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AGN1766,15/12,§20:
2 CONT S:D: The innkeeper Välaktad Olof Söderström had agreed to his neighbors Mats Matsson, Jan Jansson, Erik Jonsson, Olof Nilsson, Nils Hansson and widowed wife Margeta Andersdotter for the next. verstid had taken 300 pieces of constr
2 CONC uction timber from the village's undisturbed forest for sale, which the defendants admitted. However, the same timber is still lying unsold in the forest, unless the Innkeeper has forbidden them to remove it. Regretfully, the defe
2 CONC ndant complained about the innkeeper as if he was trying to persuade them to use the forest, the last means they have of any support for themselves and their people, and the burden of their scapegoats, preferably their weak home a
2 CONC ffairs do not suggest anything, but the forest is abundant and sufficient, which and the board knew the certificate. They will also if the clearing took place duly announced Söderström, to deserve in the same way, even though cons
2 CONC iderable timber from the forest has been used for the rebuilding of his recently burned farm. Now, because of the demand, the innkeeper Söderström was not present, nor authorized by himself for the execution of his above-mentioned
2 CONC  lawsuit, nor did he notify the due date. Because the Court of Härads, in the capacity of 12 Cap: Rbl, that Söderström, for his non-appearance, made himself 2 Daler Smts fine due, and that his counterparties pay their travel expen
2 CONC ses. But as they have not made any such claim against him either, the Court of Appeals therefore lets it depend that Söderström must show his disrepair next time, and that he has not been able to announce it to the Court. Meanwhil
2 CONC e, Afwa Villagers have not taken their cut timber to lift and use.
2 CONT
