1 NOTE {geni:about_me} TIEKEN, Hazel Eleanor (Lofdahl) - Was born in the Brockington district on Mar 14, 1926 and passed away peacefully at Parkland Place on Dec 8, 2012 with family by her side. Although Hazel grew up during difficult fi
2 CONC nancial times, she said that she never felt deprived because of her loving and caring family. Their family bond has continued to remain strong to this day. She began working as a young girl and had fond memories of her first job a
2 CONC s 'hired girl' for the Art Jung family. She worked at various jobs over the years candling eggs at Canada Packers, clerking at Frost Drug Store, the downtown Melfort Co-op, Robinson's and the Star Store. Hazel became a familiar fa
2 CONC ce to many as she worked at Broudy's Drugs for many years and finally retired after working for Ron Olson at Pharmasave. She is fondly remembered for her warm, inviting home which she always maintained, even on a clerk's salary. S
2 CONC he knew how to stretch a dollar. Hazel's marriage to Bill Tieken blessed her with three daughters to whom she was deeply devoted. She had an unconditional, selfless and sacrificing love for her family and was always there for her 
2 CONC 'girls'. Her love and support in turn gifted her with their mutual esteem, respect and never-ending gratitude. Family ties were always important so there were many happy family gatherings with all the aunts, uncles, cousins and, o
2 CONC f course, lots of food. In later years Hazel became a Jehovah's Witness and as such, served Jehovah with similar devotion and diligence. Hazel was predeceased by her parents Oscar and Severina (Malm) Lofdahl, infant brother Mervin
2 CONC , sister Violet and brother-in-law Axel Edeen, brother-in-law Art Edeen, and infant great grandson Keagen Abbott. She leaves to mourn her daughters and families; Delores & Bruce Ferguson, Kent & Carrie Ferguson, Carissa & Konrad, 
2 CONC Ron & Jocelyn Ferguson, Casey & Parker, Greg & Terri Ferguson, Alexa & Charlie, Erinn & Michael Stoll and Nathaniel; Denise & Terry Cornish, Amanda & Trevor Degenstein, Evan, Braden & Taryn, Scott & Candace Cornish, Danika & Laine
2 CONC y; Darlene & Vance Shmyr, Todd Shmyr, Lindsay & Grant Tucker, Eva & Alex, Brooke & Colby Abbott, Levin & Gunner; her sisters Elsie Edeen, and Joyce & Harry Kadachuk, and all her nieces and nephews. The Memorial Service was held fr
2 CONC om The Kingdom Hall of Jehovah's Witnesses on Wednesday, December 12, 2012 at 1:00 p.m. with Mr. Henry Lick officiating. The Honorary Pallbearers were "All of Hazel's grandchildren", the ushers were Merlin Edeen& Colette Ogren, an
2 CONC d the Memorial Book Attendant was Judy Holmes. Interment will take place at Brockington Covenant Cemetery at a later date
